{; THE ONE FLAT ERROR VALUE. Registered once, referenced everywhere:
 ; nothing throws into the run loop, so every failure an agent or the
 ; loop can encounter arrives as this shape. `kind` is the namespaced
 ; rule that failed, `message` is what a reader (agent or human) is
 ; told, and `data` carries whatever the owner of that rule attached.
 ; Producers stay closed maps of their own; this is the shared floor.
 :seon.error/data :map
 :seon.error/kind :keyword
 :seon.error/message [:string {:min 1}]
 :seon.error/value [:map {:closed true} [:seon.error/kind :seon.error/kind] [:seon.error/message :seon.error/message] [:seon.error/data {:optional true} :seon.error/data]]}
